            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0063" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-24T14:00:00-03:00">September 24, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>480. My 476, September 23, 3 p.m. In line with Aranha’s statement to me on Sunday
                    the Brazilian Chief of Staff gave Colonel Miller yesterday a secret signed
                    4–page statement regarding Brazil’s willingness to cooperate with the United
                    States in hemispheric defense. This is in reply to the memorandum prepared by
                    our War Department on the subject.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d58-f1"/> I am
                    forwarding the document and translation by air mail.<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d58-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
